WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:13.500
Arga sells iced coffee from a cart near campus. Sales are down, and he already has a cure: a discount.

2
00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:22.500
His friend asks one question first. What is the diagnosis? A cure for the wrong cause is not a cure.

3
00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:28.600
He starts with a feeling: people think my coffee is too expensive.

4
00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:31.900
A feeling cannot be tested.

5
00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:40.900
So he writes a hypothesis with a number in it. About six in ten buyers never return, because of the price.

6
00:00:40.900 --> 00:00:48.200
Before changing anything, he counts for one week. Twelve hundred people walk past the cart.

7
00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:51.500
Only three hundred notice it.

8
00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:58.400
One hundred and eighty buy, and one hundred and twenty of them come back.

9
00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:07.300
His guess was wrong. Two in three buyers return. The leak is earlier: most people never notice the cart.

10
00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:16.300
Now he lists ideas, and sorts them by impact and ease. A tall sign and a brighter canopy: high impact, easy. First.

11
00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:25.300
Moving to the main gate would help more, but it is hard. Asking for help can make a hard idea easier.

12
00:01:25.300 --> 00:01:28.300
The rest can wait.

13
00:01:28.300 --> 00:01:34.800
Then every action gets an owner and a date. The sign, by Saturday.

14
00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:37.800
The canopy, by Monday.

15
00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:45.900
And in two weeks he counts again. A plan without owners and dates is only a wish.

16
00:01:45.900 --> 00:01:49.600
Symptom, diagnosis, prescription. In that order.

17
00:01:49.600 --> 00:01:55.300
Write your guess with a number, so data can kill it.

18
00:01:55.300 --> 00:02:04.300
Now it is your turn. Pick one problem you are about to fix. Write your hypothesis with a number before you act.
